# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Rules can match by hostname.
#
# The site answers on more addresses than the one we want in search
# results. Every page already carries a canonical tag pointing at
# https://atticandember.com/, but these hosts serve full copies too, so
# tell search engines outright not to index them. Visitors on them are
# unaffected — the pages still load normally.

# Cloudflare's own address for the project, and each deploy's preview URL.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# www serves the site rather than redirecting to the bare domain. The
# proper fix is a Cloudflare redirect rule (www -> atticandember.com),
# which this repo can't set; until then, keep the duplicate out of search.
https://www.atticandember.com/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Every page, every host.
#
# Frame protection: no other site may show these pages inside a frame of
# its own (the "clickjacking" trick, where a page is laid invisibly over a
# button on someone else's site). Nothing legitimate frames this site —
# PayPal, Venmo and the order form are links and requests, not frames —
# and the site never frames itself. SAMEORIGIN rather than DENY leaves
# that door open should it ever want to. Both headers say the same thing:
# frame-ancestors is the modern form, X-Frame-Options the one older
# browsers read. This CSP restricts framing only, nothing else.
#
# HSTS: once a browser has seen it, it uses https for the site without
# trying http first. Everything here is already https-only, so nothing
# changes for a visitor except one fewer redirect on a typed address.
# Kept deliberately modest — 180 days, this hostname only (no
# includeSubDomains, so a future subdomain is never forced onto https it
# might not have), and no preload-list entry, which is hard to undo.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000
